%description:
Tests TcpSocket::setMaxSeg(), the socket option TCP_MAXSEG, on a listening
socket. The mss parameter is 1000. The server application listens at t=0 and
sets TCP_MAXSEG to 600 at t=0.2. The client connects at t=0.5: the SYN-ACK
announces an MSS of 600, as Linux limits the MSS option of each connection of
the listener, and the data of the client carry 600 bytes. Before the repair,
the SYN-ACK announced 1000, the value that the listener took at its open (the
packetdrill script mss-setsockopt-tcp_maxseg-server of inet-gpl).

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.tOpen=0.5s
*.srv_app.maxSegScript="0.2 600"  # TCP_MAXSEG on the listening socket
*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 1200"
*.*_tcp.mss = 1000

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%# the SYN-ACK announces 600...
%contains: stdout
Tcp Header Option MSS(=600) sent
%contains: stdout
Tcp Header Option MSS(=600) received, SMSS is set to 600
%# ...and the client sends 600 bytes in a segment
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A 125001:125601(600) ack 125501 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
